{"title":"🌙🍂 Fall Evening Walk: High Park & Ghost Stories 👻","startsAt":"2026-10-08T18:30:00-04:00","endsAt":"2026-10-08T20:30:00-04:00","status":"ACTIVE","type":"PHYSICAL","description":"# 🌙🍂 **Fall Evening Walk: High Park & Ghost Stories** 👻\n\n### Fall Colours, Spooky Stories & A Different Way to Spend Your Evening\n\nLooking for something a little different to do after work?\n\nJoin us for an **evening walk through High Park**, where we'll enjoy the fall colours while stopping along the way for some of the park's stranger, spookier, and downright weird stories.\nHigh Park has a long history of ghost stories and local legends.\n\nFrom stories connected to the **War of 1812** — yes, *that* War of 1812 — to tales of mysterious deaths and people who may not have completely left the park behind, there's plenty of history to make an ordinary fall walk a little more interesting.\nBut don't worry.\n\n**This isn't a terrifying ghost hunt.** 👻\n\nThink **fall colours, creepy stories, a little history, a few laughs, and just enough spooky atmosphere to make you look over your shoulder once or twice.**\n\nIt's a relaxed way to get outside after work, explore one of Toronto's most beautiful parks, and experience High Park as the daylight starts to disappear. 🍂🌙\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What We'll Do\n\nWe'll walk through **High Park**, stopping at different locations along the way while I share stories connected to the park's history and ghostly legends.\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Explore some of High Park's most interesting locations\n* Hear stories of ghosts, legends, and strange events 👻\n* Learn a little about the park's history\n* Take photos and enjoy the scenery 📸\n* Have some Halloween fun along the way 🎃\n\nWe'll keep a steady walking pace, with regular stops for storytelling.\nThe walk will remain **outside throughout** — there is no entry into buildings.\n\n***\n\n## So Let's Have Some Fun\n\nThis isn't meant to be a serious paranormal investigation.\n\nSome stories are creepy. Some are strange. Some might make you wonder whether there's actually something going on.\nAnd some are just a good excuse to tell a spooky story while walking through the fall leaves.\n\n**You don't have to believe in ghosts.**\nYou just have to enjoy a good story.\n\n***\n\n## 🍁 Fall Weather & Expectations\n\nThis is an outdoor walk, so please dress appropriately for the weather.\nHigh Park can be cool and damp in late October, so bring a warm jacket and wear comfortable walking shoes.\nWe'll be walking at a steady pace, with stops along the way for stories and photos.\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** High Park sign on the west side at Bloor Street West & High Park Avenue\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** **6:30 PM sharp**\nI will only wait **5 minutes.**\n**Early is on time. On time is late.**\n🚶 **Pace:** Steady walking pace\n🏁 **End Point:** Back where we started\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$10 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nThis is a **curated, guided storytelling experience**, rather than one of our regular group walks. The route, stories, and history have been researched and developed specifically for this experience.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 Comfortable walking shoes\n🧥 Warm fall jacket or layers\n📸 Camera or phone\n🎃 Halloween spirit\nAnd if you want to wear a costume...\n**I'm certainly not going to stop you.** 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis is great for:\n\n* People who love Halloween 🎃\n* Anyone who enjoys ghost stories\n* Fall-colour enthusiasts 🍂\n* History buffs\n* People looking for something different to do on Halloween Day\n* Anyone who enjoys a good story and a few laughs\n* People who want to meet new people while exploring Toronto\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or changed, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the fall colours.** 🍂\n**Stay for the ghost stories.** 👻\n**Leave with a new connection — if the ghosts don't get you first.** 🎃","venue":{"name":"High Park","address":"Bloor and High Park Avenue, Toronto","lat":43.65354,"lng":-79.46527,"city":"Toronto"},"fee":{"amount":10,"currency":"CAD"},"group":"No Such Thing As Bad Weather Walking & Hiking Group!","image":"https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/1/e/9/highres_535740489.jpeg"}